      "id": "9bl4nyv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Establishment of RBI"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India was established on April 1, 1935, based on the recommendations of the Hilton Young Commission.",
        "RBI was nationalized on January 1, 1949, transitioning from a private shareholders' bank to a government-owned central bank.",
        "It serves as the sole authority for issuing currency notes in India (except for one-rupee notes and coins issued by the Ministry of Finance).",
        "RBI regulates monetary policy using key quantitative instruments such as CRR, SLR, Repo Rate, and Reverse Repo Rate.",
        "It acts as the banker to the government, lender of last resort for commercial banks, and custodian of foreign exchange reserves."
      ],
      "id": "hxkpdqq"
    },
